180
00:12:16,140 --> 00:12:18,620
当然了，麦克不会作弊
Of course, Mike, you would never cheat.

181
00:12:18,960 --> 00:12:21,940
我没有作弊，你们说够了没有？
Look, I did not cheat, and I'm tired of you guys saying that I did!

182
00:12:22,942 --> 00:12:24,549
听到没有？
You got it?

183
00:12:25,760 --> 00:12:27,400
本周连续5晚.
Five nights this week...

184
00:12:27,400 --> 00:12:31,240
美国人脍炙人口的故事 将会搬上荧幕
the story that had all America reading, will have all America watching.

185
00:12:31,240 --> 00:12:32,940
18岁，修女
At 18, she was a nun.

186
00:12:33,160 --> 00:12:37,620
21岁，体操运动员，37岁，总统夫人
At 21, an acrobat. At 37, the mistress of a president.

187
00:12:39,400 --> 00:12:40,920
琼.科林是.
Joan Collins is...

188
00:12:41,527 --> 00:12:42,729
老太婆
Old.

189
00:12:47,260 --> 00:12:49,320
-麦克 -嗨
- Hi, Mike. - Hi.

190
00:12:50,200 --> 00:12:51,300
你怎么了？
What's the matter?

191
00:12:52,300 --> 00:12:53,980
你怎么知道我怎么了？
How do you know something's the matter?

192
00:12:54,540 --> 00:12:58,783
因为你没叫我“贱货”，“臭嘴”或“傻蛋”
Because you didn't say, "Hi, Fido," "Hi, Skunk-breath," or "Hi, Nerd-face."

193
00:12:59,280 --> 00:13:00,500
怎么了？
So, what is it?

194
00:13:02,214 --> 00:13:05,525
我恶梦成真了，没有人相信我
Carol, I'm living a nightmare. I mean, nobody believes me.

195
00:13:06,060 --> 00:13:09,360
邦纳，埃迪，切奇，莫里他们都不信我
Not Boner, not Eddie, not Cheech, not Murray.

196
00:13:10,500 --> 00:13:12,060
你在说什么？
What are you talking about?

197
00:13:13,460 --> 00:13:16,920
老师说我历史考试作弊
Mr. Dewitt accused me of cheating on my history exam.

198
00:13:17,520 --> 00:13:18,500
你及格了？
You passed!

199
00:13:19,480 --> 00:13:20,880
是的
Yeah, I passed.

200
00:13:21,340 --> 00:13:23,660
而且我得到了最高分
In fact, I got the highest grade in the class.

201
00:13:28,960 --> 00:13:31,420
你是说你也不相信我
Oh, oh, is this your way of saying you don't believe me either?

202
00:13:31,640 --> 00:13:33,500
-够了 -好吧!
- Stop! - Oh, oh, fine.

203
00:13:33,600 --> 00:13:36,880
不相信罢了，臭嘴!贱货!傻蛋!
Don't believe me, Skunk-breath! Fido! Nerd-face!

204
00:13:43,180 --> 00:13:45,960
爸!妈!看见你们真好
Mom! Dad! How great to see you!

205
00:13:46,325 --> 00:13:48,677
-嗨 -他是在跟我们说话吗？
- Hey. - Is he talking to us?

206
00:13:48,680 --> 00:13:51,640
我信任你们能让我快乐
I mean, just knowing that I can count on you guys makes me feel happy.

207
00:13:51,880 --> 00:13:54,640
这种信任是双向的
Oh, the giddiness is completely mutual, Mike.

208
00:13:54,700 --> 00:13:56,080
谢谢
Hey, you're welcome.

209
00:13:56,080 --> 00:13:57,700
-发烧了？ -妈
- Do you have a fever? - Mom.

210
00:13:59,060 --> 00:14:01,700
麦姬，我说这是不是.
Say, Maggie, you don't suppose this has anything to do...

211
00:14:01,700 --> 00:14:03,520
兴最近的历史考试有关呢？
with his recent history test, do you?

212
00:14:03,843 --> 00:14:06,494
说到这个刚好
You know, I'm darn glad you brought that up, Dad.

213
00:14:07,180 --> 00:14:08,460
我还是先坐下
I'd better sit down.

214
00:14:09,120 --> 00:14:09,760
怎么了？
What happened?

215
00:14:10,600 --> 00:14:13,600
考试本身没什么好说的
Well, there's not too much to be said about the test itself.

216
00:14:14,300 --> 00:14:15,200
还是说说看吧
Say it anyway.

217
00:14:17,980 --> 00:14:18,900
及格了
I passed.

218
00:14:20,000 --> 00:14:21,200
-完全及格了？ -太好了
- Completely? - Yeah.

219
00:14:22,100 --> 00:14:24,900
-麦克，好啊 -恭喜
- Hey, all right, Mike. - Congratulations.

220
00:14:24,960 --> 00:14:27,500
额外的温习果然奏效
I knew that that little extra studying would pay off.

221
00:14:27,800 --> 00:14:29,158
谢谢
Thanks.

222
00:14:29,600 --> 00:14:31,440
不过我有坏消息
But I do have some bad news...

223
00:14:32,720 --> 00:14:34,720
爸，你还是先坐下
and I think you better sit down for this, Dad.

224
00:14:34,860 --> 00:14:36,160
麦克，说吧
Just say what it is, Mike.

225
00:14:36,480 --> 00:14:38,300
我认为你还是先坐下吧
I have a feeling you should sit.

226
00:14:41,820 --> 00:14:45,940
我说出这件事后，你们将会很气愤
Now what I'm about to tell you is going to get both of you quite angry...

227
00:14:46,040 --> 00:14:49,020
甚至会对老师的做法.
and you will be outraged at the shoddy treatment...

228
00:14:49,020 --> 00:14:50,500
感到生气，勃然大怒
I have received from Mr. Dewitt.

229
00:14:51,590 --> 00:14:54,640
不过你要承诺，不能兴冲冲地.
But I want your word that you're not gonna go off half-cocked...

230
00:14:54,640 --> 00:14:56,260
要让他被学校开除
trying to get this guy fired or something.

231
00:14:56,260 --> 00:14:58,920
我承诺不会这样
I promise to be fully-cocked, Mike.

232
00:15:01,160 --> 00:15:06,640
老师指控我.
Now, Mr. Dewitt accused me...

233
00:15:06,640 --> 00:15:07,200
考试作弊
of cheating.

234
00:15:10,400 --> 00:15:13,680
-冷静点! -我很冷静
- Now just calm down! - I'm in control.

235
00:15:13,800 --> 00:15:15,060
我没有作弊
I did not cheat!

236
00:15:15,640 --> 00:15:18,200
老师为什么会这样做？
Now why would Mr. Dewitt think that?

237
00:15:19,440 --> 00:15:22,960
整个下午我也在问自己这个问题
You know, I have been asking myself that same question all afternoon.

238
00:15:23,200 --> 00:15:24,800
那你想到些什么？
Well, what'd you come up with, Mike?

239
00:15:24,800 --> 00:15:28,300
也许他想不到我成绩那么好
I don't know. I guess he didn't expect me to do that well on the test.

240
00:15:28,860 --> 00:15:31,280
好？成绩好？
Well? You did well? He did well.

241
00:15:32,480 --> 00:15:33,640
有多好？
How well?

242
00:15:35,000 --> 00:15:37,260
我很少在意分数
I rarely pay attention to the grades.

243
00:15:38,200 --> 00:15:38,760
-多少分？70？
-75？ - What'd you get? 70? - 75?

244
00:15:41,040 --> 00:15:42,241
-这个..
-80？ - Well... - 80?

245
00:15:42,241 --> 00:15:43,609
-这..
-85？ - See... - 85?

246
00:15:43,609 --> 00:15:45,077
-其实..
-90？ - Actually... - 90?

247
00:15:45,077 --> 00:15:45,256
-4 -94!

248
00:15:45,256 --> 00:15:46,900
- Four. - 94!

249
00:15:46,900 --> 00:15:49,360
麦克.西弗，我为你感到羞耻!
Why, Michael Seaver, I'm ashamed of you!

250
00:15:50,980 --> 00:15:54,620
-你怎么能作弊! -我没有作弊!
- How could you cheat? - I did not cheat.

251
00:15:55,080 --> 00:15:56,540
满分是100分的那种94？
Is this 94 out of 100?

252
00:15:58,960 --> 00:16:01,760
我发誓我没有作弊
I swear to you I did not cheat.

253
00:16:02,094 --> 00:16:04,507
否则五雷轰顶
Dad, I give you my word of honor.

254
00:16:06,131 --> 00:16:08,943
我相信你
Well, I believe you.

255
00:16:11,160 --> 00:16:12,160
-是吗？ -是吗？
- Really? - Really?

256
00:16:13,600 --> 00:16:16,820
要是儿子都发誓了，我们得相信
Well, if our son gives us his word, we've gotta believe him.

257
00:16:21,660 --> 00:16:22,540
说得对
You're right.

258
00:16:23,440 --> 00:16:24,420
麦克，我相信你
I believe you, Mike.

259
00:16:26,285 --> 00:16:28,754
谢谢，我就知道能信任你们
Well, thanks. I knew I could count on you guys.

260
00:16:28,754 --> 00:16:33,276
我为我平时让你们 痛不欲生的行为道歉
I am sorry for every miserable thing I've ever done to make your world a living hell.

261
00:16:33,960 --> 00:16:35,760
对不起，我刚才怀疑你
And I'm sorry I doubted you, Mike...

262
00:16:35,760 --> 00:16:39,080
但站在我的角度 你也能理解这事很难相信
but it's a tough story to believe if you put yourself in my shoes.

263
00:16:40,580 --> 00:16:43,100
妈妈的鞋子可写不下所有答案
Mom's shoes aren't big enough for all the answers.

264
00:16:45,960 --> 00:16:48,500
对了，鞋子的事，谢谢
All right, the shoes. Thanks, Benny.

265
00:16:48,900 --> 00:16:51,100
我忘了最有趣的部分
I forgot to tell you guys the funniest part.

266
00:16:53,660 --> 00:16:55,580
你们一定会喜欢听
You guys are gonna love this.

267
00:17:03,722 --> 00:17:04,890
麦克？
Mike?

268
00:17:04,890 --> 00:17:09,044
-本尼迪克特.阿诺德将军？ -不，本.西弗
- Benedict Arnold. - No, Ben Seaver.

269
00:17:10,400 --> 00:17:11,480
走开
Get away.

270
00:17:13,240 --> 00:17:14,780
吃饭吗？
Want some dinner?

271
00:17:15,220 --> 00:17:17,420
我再也不吃.
No, I am no longer eating the food...

272
00:17:17,420 --> 00:17:19,880
那些认为我撒谎的人的食物
that has been paid for by the people who think I'm a liar.

273
00:17:20,520 --> 00:17:21,260
那些是什么？
Then what are those?

274
00:17:22,580 --> 00:17:24,380
这事要循序渐进嘛
Okay, so I'm easing into it.

275
00:17:25,260 --> 00:17:26,580
你要干什么？
What do you want anyway?

276
00:17:26,780 --> 00:17:29,620
麦克，我不知道会带来这么多麻烦
Mike, I didn't mean to get you in such big trouble.

277
00:17:30,349 --> 00:17:31,811
没关系
It's okay.

278
00:17:32,020 --> 00:17:33,980
我也知道鞋子的事难以接受
I knew the shoes would be too much for them.

279
00:17:35,020 --> 00:17:36,400
已经一整天了
It's been like that all day.

280
00:17:36,720 --> 00:17:39,620
全校的人，连邦纳也是
Everybody at school, even Boner.

281
00:17:39,620 --> 00:17:42,840
去年我还成功骗了他，我是外星人
I mean, last year I actually convinced the man I was an alien.

282
00:17:45,440 --> 00:17:48,260
人们都预想我要作弊
Ben, people are acting like they expect me to cheat.

283
00:17:48,680 --> 00:17:50,000
把我当作是个臭小子
Like I'm that kind of low scuzzball.

284
00:17:51,480 --> 00:17:52,700
我相信你
I believe you.

285
00:17:53,272 --> 00:17:54,480
什么？
What?

286
00:17:54,480 --> 00:17:57,760
不管是真是假，你说什么我都相信你
Whatever you say I believe it, whether it's the truth or not.

287
00:17:59,745 --> 00:18:01,620
告诉你最怪的感觉
Well, I'll tell you something weird.

288
00:18:01,620 --> 00:18:04,620
爸爸妈妈相信我那一刻
That moment when Mom and Dad believed me...

289
00:18:05,240 --> 00:18:06,520
事情好好的
everything was okay.

290
00:18:09,020 --> 00:18:12,320
天哪!我竟然在乎他们对我的看法
My God! I actually care what they think about me.

291
00:18:13,420 --> 00:18:15,500
我也在乎他们对我的看法
I care what they think about me.

292
00:18:16,580 --> 00:18:19,200
但你才9岁，这是正常的
Well, you're nine. That's okay to feel that way at nine.

293
00:18:20,200 --> 00:18:23,240
我15岁了，我应该感到父母是废物
But I'm 15. I'm supposed to think my parents are scum.

294
00:18:24,040 --> 00:18:25,040
你肯定？
Are you sure?

295
00:18:25,680 --> 00:18:28,740
这是众所周知的，电视上也能看到
Yeah, everybody knows that. It's on TV all the time.

296
00:18:29,240 --> 00:18:30,460
我相信你
I believe you.

297
00:18:36,020 --> 00:18:37,340
你在这
There you are.

298
00:18:38,460 --> 00:18:40,040
外面很冷
You're gonna freeze out here.

299
00:18:41,160 --> 00:18:43,380
心中的怒火让我温暖
No, I've got my anger to keep me warm.

300
00:18:44,960 --> 00:18:46,320
我可以分担吗？
Could you share some with me?

301
00:18:50,800 --> 00:18:52,840
杰森，我有话对你说
Jason, I have something to tell you.

302
00:18:53,360 --> 00:18:56,060
其实不想说的，现在麦克出卖了你.
Now I didn't want to tell you, but since you're feeling betrayed by Mike...

303
00:18:56,100 --> 00:18:57,520
你需要一些好消息振奋一下
I figure you'd need some good news.

304
00:18:58,340 --> 00:19:00,760
你不是麦克的父亲
You're not really Mike's father.

305
00:19:04,700 --> 00:19:06,060
你猜我在想什么？
Well, you know what I've been thinking?

306
00:19:06,740 --> 00:19:08,680
麦克能在你面前撒谎.
That when Mike looked you in the eye and lied...

307
00:19:08,700 --> 00:19:11,280
让你质疑你教导孩子诚实的方法
it made you question your whole approach to teaching our kids...

308
00:19:11,280 --> 00:19:13,000
这种方法对不对
the value of truth and honesty.

309
00:19:13,600 --> 00:19:16,340
你疑问通过举例来教导.
And you're wondering if instead of encouraging them by example...

310
00:19:16,460 --> 00:19:18,820
到不如换成用惩罚来教导
a little fear of punishment might have been even more effective.

311
00:19:19,220 --> 00:19:21,660
也许你还记得麦克8岁的时候
And you're probably remembering the time when Mike was eight...

312
00:19:21,660 --> 00:19:24,260
他撒谎没有弄脏新地毯，我要打他
and he lied about finger-painting the new rug, and I wanted to spank him...

313
00:19:24,260 --> 00:19:26,100
你却说服了我应该跟他讲道理
but you convinced me that reasoning with him was better.

314
00:19:26,820 --> 00:19:28,160
这你是怎么做到的？
How do you do that?

315
00:19:29,820 --> 00:19:31,420
这不算什么
Oh, it's not all that amazing.

316
00:19:31,420 --> 00:19:33,560
我看你也知道我在想什么
I bet you know what I'm thinking right now.

317
00:19:34,620 --> 00:19:37,480
你也许在想虽然我们对麦克很失望.
You're probably thinking that no matter how disappointed we both are in Mike...

318
00:19:37,520 --> 00:19:38,620
我们还是很疼他
that we love him dearly.

319
00:19:39,220 --> 00:19:42,280
我们会尽力把他塑造成诚实的人
And that we'll do our best to mold him into an honest man.

320
00:19:43,060 --> 00:19:46,580
若是不成功，也可以让他当政客
And that even if we fail, he can always have a productive life in politics.

321
00:19:51,300 --> 00:19:55,480
麦克，坦白从宽
Mike, Mr. Dewitt will go a lot easier on you, if you just admit what you did.

322
00:19:56,400 --> 00:19:58,700
-我不在乎 -我们在乎
- I don't care. - Well, we do.

323
00:19:59,200 --> 00:20:01,200
你就装作在乎我们的感受好吗？
Couldn't you at least pretend that you care what we think?

324
00:20:01,767 --> 00:20:03,635
没有人相信我
Sure, but nobody'll believe me.

325
00:20:03,635 --> 00:20:06,833
-为什么要相信你？ -因为我没有作弊
- But why should anyone? - Because I didn't cheat.

326
00:20:07,320 --> 00:20:08,720
算了，没关系
Forget it. It doesn't matter.

327
00:20:09,820 --> 00:20:12,000
我们应该相信你初一时.
Well, should we have believed you back in the seventh grade...

328
00:20:12,000 --> 00:20:15,380
你说的成绩单上的“差”是指“差点满分”？
when you tried to tell us that the D on your report card stood for "darn good"?

329
00:20:16,640 --> 00:20:19,000
初二时你骗老师.
And what about in the eighth grade when you told the school...

330
00:20:19,000 --> 00:20:21,900
说你是犹太人，于是多了几天假期？
your name was Seaverman so you could take the Jewish holidays off?

331
00:20:23,789 --> 00:20:26,890
-就说这个星期.. -好吧，好吧
- And, Mike, just this week... - Okay, okay.

332
00:20:27,120 --> 00:20:29,280
有时候.
All right, sometimes...

333
00:20:29,960 --> 00:20:30,780
我是撒谎了
I lie.

334
00:20:31,380 --> 00:20:35,380
但撒谎和“撒谎”是不同的
But there's a big difference between being a liar and being a liar.

335
00:20:35,760 --> 00:20:38,740
你们应该知道我何时说真话
I mean, you guys should know when I'm telling the truth.

336
00:20:39,180 --> 00:20:41,220
你们是怎样的父母？
What kind of parents are you anyway?

337
00:20:43,242 --> 00:20:44,946
失望的父母
Disappointed.

338
00:20:47,012 --> 00:20:48,945
想知道真相？
You wanna know the truth?

339
00:20:49,440 --> 00:20:51,360
我告诉你真相
Okay, I'll tell you the truth.

340
00:20:52,660 --> 00:20:55,940
我是准备作弊 我以为这是唯一的出路
Yeah, I was going to cheat. I figured it was the only way.

341
00:20:56,500 --> 00:20:59,580
于是我熬夜把东西写在鞋底
So I was up half the night copying all that stuff onto my shoes...

342
00:20:59,858 --> 00:21:02,328
这考试不能不过
'cause I had to pass the test.

343
00:21:02,400 --> 00:21:06,620
但不知为何，不仅写在鞋子上 更写进脑袋里了
But somehow it didn't just go on my shoes. It got in my head, too.

344
00:21:07,299 --> 00:21:09,167
我也吓了一跳
It sure blew me away.

345
00:21:10,580 --> 00:21:14,920
当我要看答案时，我不用看也知道了
But when it came time to look for the answers, I didn't have to.

346
00:21:15,820 --> 00:21:16,900
我都知道
I knew them.

347
00:21:17,620 --> 00:21:19,660
麦克，我也想相信你
Well, I'd like to believe you, Mike.

348
00:21:20,946 --> 00:21:22,282
嗯
Yeah.

349
00:21:22,580 --> 00:21:25,220
但你得承认，你并不像那种.
You have to admit you're not exactly the kind of guy who has a reputation...

350
00:21:25,220 --> 00:21:28,820
能记住林肯是第17任总统的人
for knowing things like Abraham Lincoln was the 17th President.

351
00:21:30,240 --> 00:21:32,280
爸，他是第16任总统
Yeah, he was the 16th President, Dad.

352
00:21:32,457 --> 00:21:35,927
-格兰特是第17任 -不，格兰特是第18任
- Yes, Grant was 17th. - No, Grant was the 18th.

353
00:21:35,927 --> 00:21:37,520
约翰逊才是第17任
See, Johnson was 17th.

354
00:21:37,520 --> 00:21:40,880
林肯在1865年4月14日被刺后 他成为了总统
He became President after Lincoln was assassinated on April 14, 1865.

355
00:21:47,740 --> 00:21:51,620
西弗先生，西弗太太，我是得威特老师 谢谢你们能来
Dr. And Mrs. Seaver, I'm Willis Dewitt. Glad you could come.

356
00:21:51,780 --> 00:21:53,440
我们谈正事吧
Why don't we get right down to business?

357
00:21:54,146 --> 00:21:55,625
好的
Absolutely.

358
00:21:56,000 --> 00:21:58,740
麦克考试时并没有作弊
Mike did not cheat on this examination, Mr. Dewitt...

359
00:21:58,760 --> 00:22:00,300
这事可不能含糊
and it's important that we clear that up.

360
00:22:00,480 --> 00:22:02,340
光看脚底下的答案.
And it would have been so easy for him to do...

361
00:22:02,340 --> 00:22:04,920
这也太没意思了吧？
what with all the answers written on the bottom of his shoes.

362
00:22:10,520 --> 00:22:13,860
老师，谢谢你能让麦克重考
I want to thank you, Mr. Dewitt, for letting Mike take this make-up test.

363
00:22:14,200 --> 00:22:14,860
没问题
No problem.

364
00:22:15,460 --> 00:22:19,280
希望他知道意图作弊和作弊 是同等严重的
I think he's learned now that intending to cheat was just as bad as cheating itself.

365
00:22:20,220 --> 00:22:22,200
我前期也是这么说我
That's what my ex-wife said in court.

366
00:22:24,860 --> 00:22:26,180
他要考试呢
He's trying to take a test.

367
00:22:41,580 --> 00:22:42,520
今晚有什么节目？
What's on tonight?

368
00:22:43,840 --> 00:22:45,580
琼.科林系列的第二集
It's the second night of that Joan Collins mini-series.

369
00:22:46,360 --> 00:22:47,180
也许很好看
That might be interesting.

370
00:22:47,880 --> 00:22:50,680
今晚琼要离开教皇，嫁给一个建筑工人
Tonight Joan leaves the Pope to marry a bricklayer.

371
00:22:52,304 --> 00:22:55,160
麦克错过好节目了
Mike'll be sorry he's missing that one.

372
00:22:55,220 --> 00:22:57,140
麦克在哪？整晚没见到他
Where is Mike anyway? I haven't seen him all evening.

373
00:22:57,180 --> 00:22:59,660
他在楼上准备明天的法语考试
Well, he's upstairs studying for his French test tomorrow.

374
00:23:00,120 --> 00:23:03,120
这次他也许相通了
You know, I really think we got through to him this time.

375
00:23:54,647 --> 00:23:55,786
[zeroxia@gmail.com] 2006.04.01
